what REDS %782: nib_honesty gathers advertised hashes with grep -oE '[0-9a-f]{10}' and hex admits the decimals, so Diffuser's LCG account (1103515245, 2147483648) reads as two floating commit claims and the guard stands RED on a healthy tree for every ship. Rule the recognition question the row leaves open: POSITION decides the gate where the card names a key (Git nib, checkpoint, walk-back nib immediately preceding), SHAPE decides where it does not (a hex run carrying a letter is a hash claim), and RESOLUTION classifies what shape cannot -- an all-decimal run in bare prose is read as a numeral unless the object store resolves it. Measured on this history: 52 of 5138 commits carry an all-decimal short hash, one in 99, so a letter-only rule would drop real hashes silently and that residue is named rather than hidden.
