what The control-in-population census reports MEMBERSHIP -- a guard's population holds a tracked file of its own family -- and names the exact question as out of reach: whether the guard's ANSWER moves when that control leaves the index. Last lap ran that perturbation ad hoc in a pen over the 37 scans the census could enumerate and threw the script away, so 13 moved verdicts stand on an instrument this tree does not carry. Seat the probe as tracked equipment: for a named scan with a tracked family control, run it in a detached worktree with the control tracked, again with the control removed from the index, and report unmoved | moved | verdict_flipped from the two outputs. Then run it over the nine no-git-population scans the census reads as structurally unmeasured -- each roots a find at the repository root or under tools/, so each CAN reach a control and none is enumerable statically, because every find root in that class is a loop or per-scan variable rather than a resolvable path. The card's own line says twelve; the root test says nine, and the correction rides with the reading.
